    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0449" n="343" xml:id="pg343"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Pedro Montt to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Chile</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send you a copy of the
                    telegram which was received last night from my Government, and of which I spoke
                    to you in our interview to day, whereby I am informed of the progress of the
                    proceedings now being held at Valparaiso on account of the lamentable occurrence
                    of October 16.</p>
                <p>As appears from the proceedings which have already been made public, all the
                    North Americans, with the exception of two, declare that the police did their
                    duty and make no charges against them whatever.</p>
                <p>With sentiments, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pedro Montt</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d331-a1.xml" xpointer="d331-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
